WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.376
- We could be walking down the hallway. 

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:02.919
He can be coming this way and I come that way.

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:05.171
And I’m supposed to be the star receiver, you’re the star quarterback.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.923
You look down at your phone, 

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:07.882
so guess what I do?

00:00:07.882 --> 00:00:09.926
I put my head down, and we walk right past each other 

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:10.760
and won't say nothing.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:17.642
♪♪♪ 

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.186
- You had a long career in the NFL. 

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:20.854
- Uh-huh.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.647
- And a lot of people know you for taking it back to the crib. 

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:26.317
Special Teams, dude, there are very few, if any, that were better than you.

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.070
Only person I can think of is really Dante Hall that would be in that same category, 

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.406
and if you take that as an insult, correct me if I’m wrong.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:33.867
How do you take that?

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.701
- Insult.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.119
- Do you think there's anybody better than you as a returner?

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:37.078
- Not what I did.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.330
I do think there’s some good guys out there. 

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.707
Some great returners out there. 

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:44.002
But I don’t think anybody had done it the way I did.

00:00:44.002 --> 00:00:46.880
- People believe return specialists like Brian Mitchell and yourself 

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.881
belong in the Hall of Fame.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.882
- Right, right, right.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.718
- Do you think Brian Mitchell and Devin Hester should have a space in Canton? 

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:54.512
- I think so, but I think they all waitin’ on me first to make it.

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:57.807
Once I’m in, I think some of the other returners will get in.  

00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:00.685
But to be fair to myself, I do feel like I should be the first one in.

00:01:00.685 --> 00:01:04.647
- The other question I’ve always had about your career 
was why you weren’t used more as a wide receiver.

00:01:04.647 --> 00:01:06.524
Especially in Chicago, it seemed like 

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:08.735
those first couple years, they were kinda using you 

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.488
in a similar way that, you know, guys like Cordarrelle Patterson right now—

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.655
- Right, right, right.
- You know, are being used.

00:01:12.655 --> 00:01:13.281
- Right.

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:15.366
- What happened there? Why didn’t you get more opportunities at wide receiver?

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.368
What’d you feel the real reason behind that was?

00:01:17.368 --> 00:01:19.370
- So, my third year, that’s when I 

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:20.997
redid a new contract 

00:01:20.997 --> 00:01:22.749
and became the No. 1 receiver.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:25.043
That’s the same year we brought in Jay Cutler.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:27.545
He’s not really a sociable guy. 

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.964
He’s not a talker, you know what I mean?

00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:31.800
He picks one or two guys, 

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.844
and he just leeches on ‘em and separates himself from everybody.

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:38.056
As a quarterback, like, I’d tell him to his face today that,

00:01:38.056 --> 00:01:39.015
to me, 

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:40.934
my years in the NFL—I played 11 years. 

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.937
He’s the best quarterback when it comes to 

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.189
accuracy, power, knowledge of the game.

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.941
The best quarterback, hands down, I ever played with.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.568
Now when it comes to leadership, 

00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:51.694
the worst.

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:52.445
- The worst?

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.071
- The worst.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:54.072
- He don’t know how to communicate.

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:55.657
He don’t know how to get his teammates involved. 

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:56.658
For me to be, like, 

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.661
at that time, one of the No. 1 or No. 2 receivers, like, 

00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:01.955
you supposed to have my back regardless.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:04.207
- So clearly y’all didnt have the best relationship.

00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:04.749
- Nah.

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:08.628
- I feel like personally, the only person I feel has 
been cool with Jay Cutler is Brandon Marshall. 

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:13.758
Correct me if I’m wrong. It just, it feels like ever 
other person has some sort of story or some sort of 

00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:15.927
disagreement or at odds with Jay Cutler.

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:17.011
- That’s true that you mention that. 

00:02:17.011 --> 00:02:19.180
So B. Marshall voiced his opinion a lot. 

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:19.848
- Mmhmm. 

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.474
- Him and Jay Cutler came in together 

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:22.892
at Denver. 

00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:25.520
They was, like, bros. Like, they argued. 

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:28.064
B. Marshall would cuss him out, let him know how he feels.

00:02:28.064 --> 00:02:30.024
I’m on the sideline. We in practice, right? 

00:02:30.024 --> 00:02:32.902
They doin’ pregame, warming up, tossing and throwing the ball.

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:35.196
Jay Cutler and B. Marshall get into it. 

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.073
B. Marshall yells out, 

00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:39.534
“I made you!” You know what I mean? 

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:42.328
“If it weren’t for me, you wouldn’t be Jay Cutler! 

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.289
All these Pro Bowls and stuff, you got this cuz of me!”

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:47.500
I was lookin at Julius Peppers, he’s looking at me. I say, “Listen here,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.918
we finna make a bet.” 

00:02:48.918 --> 00:02:52.255
I say, “I bet you Jay Cutler throw B. Marshall the ball. 

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:54.674
If he throw him the ball, you give me $50.

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.510
If he don’t throw to B. Marshall, I’mma give you $100.”

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:58.928
- That's how confident you were?

00:02:58.928 --> 00:03:00.930
- That’s how confident I was. I said, “I know how this practice finna go.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.057
He mad at Jay, but Jay Cutler finna give him the ball the whole practice.”

00:03:03.057 --> 00:03:04.017
- What you walk away from? 

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.018
- We stopped betting. 

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:06.644
The betting stopped.

00:03:06.644 --> 00:03:09.272
We stopped the bet at 21 passes. 

00:03:09.272 --> 00:03:11.065
He threw—
- 21 to Marshall?

00:03:11.065 --> 00:03:13.234
- He threw 21 passes to B. Marshall.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.611
21 straight.

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:17.071
I looked at the coaches like, “Are you really fucking kidding?” 

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:19.490
And wasn’t nobody saying nothin’. That was what really pissed me off. 

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:20.491
21 times straight, bro.

00:03:20.491 --> 00:03:21.701
- That’s like a rack you got from that.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.912
- We stopped betting. He said, “Bro, I don’t even wanna bet no more, bro.”

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.622
- He gonna have to give you a game check at some point.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:26.915
- It was like 21 times straight, bro. 

00:03:26.915 --> 00:03:29.834
- What was Julius Peppers saying? After 21 times, and you looking straight at Julius.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:33.129
- He was just laughing. He was like, “I can’t believe this, bro.” 

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.547
Like, “I can’t believe this, bro.” 

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.675
Like, “This really what your offense got going on?” Like, “Bro, listen.”

00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:39.135
They argue like cats and dogs.

00:03:39.135 --> 00:03:42.180
That’s why B. Marshall give Jay Cutler all the praise, man.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.264
- Go ‘head and get this shot in real quick

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:46.726
